TO : WSI
CC : ASI, Others
FM : CCE


Before we provide the background of =93Force Majeure Charge=94 to the custo=
mers in origin side, please be sure to discuss the feasibility of =93Force =
Majeure Charge=94 implementation again without any risk against MOT=92s inv=
estigation against carrier=92s imposing surcharges together with origin(ASI=
) with checking other carriers=92 actions and let CCE know your discussion =
result/opinion as soon as possible.
Without the sufficient checking the customers=92 feedback, customers might =
misunderstand our intention.
Furthermore, currently, the MOT has launched an investigation into allegati=
ons by the China Shippers Association (CSA) that shipping lines in China ar=
e colluding and imposing unreasonable surcharges on China exports.
MOT has tasked the Shanghai Shipping Exchange (SSE) to carry out this inves=
tigation.  SSE requested a meeting with ISAA (and all other discussion agre=
ements) as part of their research and investigation.
In this regards, we definitely need to be very careful and exercise discret=
ion in how you apply miscellaneous surcharges in China.
Even thought the background of =93Force Majeure Charge=94 itself seems reas=
onable due to the current INNAH terminal situation, we may be exposed to be=
 the danger of the main target by MOT=92s investigation without securing ve=
ry clear and reasonable rationale about =93Force Majeure Charge=94 implemen=
tation by ourselves.

